-->

## SYNOPSIS
`dsudo [OPTIONS]`

## DESCRIPTION
Runs `sudo` submitting the account's default empty password.

Forwards all environment variables and parameters to `sudo`.

Sets `SUDO_ASKPASS=/usr/libexec/derivative-base-files/askpass-default`
which submits an empty-by-default `sudo_password` unless environment
variable `sudo_password` is already set to something else (e.g.
`sudo_password=changeme dsudo ...` for a legacy image).

Useful for headless/automated root, where a plain `sudo -n` is refused
because an empty password still has to be submitted.

